{"repositoryId":403437523,"availability":"available","full":"cretucosmin3/Blossom","name":"Blossom","description":"Cross platform web like UI framework","category":"Developer tools","language":"C#","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2021-09-06T00:01:27Z","updated":"2026-10-16T21:34:36Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://www.nuget.org/packages/SkiaGameRendering","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:13:11.306Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T07:13:11.306Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T07:13:11.306Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T07:13:11.306Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A C# UI framework for desktop apps and game UI, drawn on the GPU with Skia.","Blossom is a retained-mode UI framework for C#. A UI is a tree of VisualElements inside a View; Blossom redraws only the areas that changed and doesn't render at all while the app is idle. There's no HTML or CSS. The core handles layout, styling, input and drawing, and controls like buttons, text fields and sliders are built on top of it, as in the demos below."],"features":["As a desktop app. Blossom opens the window (GLFW through Silk.NET) and handles input.","Inside a game. Your engine owns the window and the loop. Blossom draws into a texture you give it and takes input you pass in. The core libraries don't depend on Silk.NET or GLFW."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cretucosmin3/Blossom/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"29dc4f5f03a95488a7e813ffe62a8bff7038eed16feeb66e172be2179232c1c3","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T07:13:11.417Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:13:11.417Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A C# UI framework for desktop apps and game UI, drawn on the GPU with Skia.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cretucosmin3/Blossom/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"29dc4f5f03a95488a7e813ffe62a8bff7038eed16feeb66e172be2179232c1c3","source